{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-reeb-u1-chart-swap","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:reeb-u1-chart-swap","kind":"proposition","title":"Chart-swap $U(1)$ equals the Reeb $U(1)$ as subgroups of $\\mathrm{Aut}(\\mathbb{P}(V))$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-contact-affine-chart","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-affine-chart-origin-of-i-and-q","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/thm-categorical-reeb-exists","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-categorical-reeb-brings","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-reeb-su2","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-frobenius-hopf-substrate","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-i-as-braiding-orientation","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-projective-line-object","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-quantum-observable-universe"],"tags":["reeb","chart-transition","wick-rotation","imaginary-unit","u1-action","knot-operator","categorical-coordinate"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.ChartSwap.eqReeb","text":"reeb-u1-chart-swap.md","leanSource":"reeb-u1-chart-swap.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<p><a id=\"prop:reeb-u1-chart-swap\"></a>\n<strong>Proposition.</strong> <em>Chart-swap <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">U(1)</code> equals the Reeb <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">U(1)</code> as subgroups of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{Aut}(\\mathbb{P}(V))</code></em></p>\n<p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)</code> be a quantum observable universe. As subgroups of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{Aut}_{\\mathbf{C}}(\\mathbb{P}(V))</code>:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\langle \\rho_{\\theta_q} : \\theta_q \\in U(1) \\rangle = \\langle \\phi_t : t \\in \\mathbb{R} \\rangle = T_q.</code></pre>\n<p>The chart-swap one-parameter subgroup and the Reeb flow subgroup coincide as the image of the maximal torus <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T_q</code>.</p>\n"}
